								| Reflection
				//
					<div class="project-for project-detail-item project-deliverables">
						<h2>Deliverables</h2>
						<a class="button-small" target="_blank"
						href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DHk9P7hJ0ig">Trailer</a>
						<a class="button-small" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DHk9P7hJ0ig">Final
						Report</a>
						<a class="button-small" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DHk9P7hJ0ig">Data
						Canvas</a>
						<a class="button-small" target="_blank"
						href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DHk9P7hJ0ig">Website</a>
						</div>
			#article
				section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="what_it_is")
					h2.heading-underline What it is
					.explanation-wrapper
						div
							p.summary-text
								| The BC Healthcare Hub is a mobile application prototype that supports learning about and using British Columbia's healthcare system.
							p.summary-text
								| Our goal for this project was to ideate, design, and create a fully interactive prototype for international students arriving to BC.
							p.summary-text
								| Content and visual design, system logic, and user testing were all expected
								|   of us. Highlights of my work included developing the underlying interface system of the MSP form,
								|   conducting thematic analysis on user study data, and creating most of the application in ProtoPie.
						.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Final design
							img(
								alt="Winner-takes-all system" 
								width="2560" 
								height="2464" 
								src="../../img/design/bc/final_interface.webp"
								)
				section.wrapper-padding.article-section(id="qualitative_interviews")
					h2.heading-underline The issue with qualitative interviews
					.explanation-wrapper
						div
							p
								| Three quarters through the project, user testing was conducted with our first prototype. After my
								|    teammates conducted the user study, we had several pages of interview notes that contained tangents,
								|    overly general remarks, and other fluff. We needed to get to the juicy, tangible praise and
								|    criticism that interviewees provided so we can understand the state of our prototype. I was tasked
								|    to return valuable, actionable insights from the study’s qualitative interview notes.
							p
								| I chose to use thematic analysis as we wanted to identify common issues users had with the app and
								|    understand them as high-level problems within our design strategies of the app. Thematic analysis’s
								|    benefits of coding, theming, and defining problems helped in our goals.
						.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Notes from user testing interviews
							img(
								alt="Screenshots of document notes from user testing interviews" 
								width="2560" 
								height="2210" 
								src="../../img/design/bc/user_testing_documents.webp"
								)
				section#thematic_analysis.wrapper-padding.article-section
					h2.heading-underline Thematic analysis
					.explanation-wrapper
						div
							p
								| I began to copy the raw interview notes to a Figma document, chopping multi-topic sentences into
								|    single topic snippets and grouping similar quotes together, coding the information. I then
								|    abstracted the data into separate themes of the application’s systems and design. This
								|    did not yield any significant insights as each theme encompassed too many data points, resulting in
								|    overly generalized outcomes. However, I found that many of the children of each theme shared
								|    underlying similarities of visual design, content design and strategy, and system logic. So, I took
								|    the initial sections and broke them down into these smaller categories.

						.subheading
							h3.heading-underline Two iterations of thematic analysis theming
							.images-together
								img(
									alt="Screenshot of digital sticky notes grouped together by a few themes" 
									width="2560" 
									height="2210" 
									src="../../img/design/bc/thematic_analysis_1st_round.webp"
									)
								img(
									alt="Screenshot of digital sticky notes grouped together by a lot of themes" 
									width="2560" 
									height="2210" 
									src="../../img/design/bc/thematic_analysis_2nd_round.webp"
									)
				section#reflection.wrapper-padding.article-section
					h2.heading-underline Reflection
					p
						| This revealed some interesting outcomes: some themes were very specific (for example, warning and error
						|   icons and colours) while others were very generalized (e.g. UI design). This level of detail of the themes
						|   showed us the most common issues that were brought up and allowed us to prioritize certain issues. Finally,
						|   to visualize this in a more cohesive manner, I placed these themes them into a Venn diagram of design,
						|   system, and content. This allowed us to communicate our issues clearly in the weekly presentation
						|   and outline solutions we will use to address each of these themes.
					p
						| The outcome of the thematic analysis helped us streamline what iterations needed to be prioritized leading
						|  up to the deadline of the project.
		// Footer
		include includes/footer